{
  "id": "thresholds-and-expectation-thresholds",
  "title": "Thresholds and expectation thresholds",
  "description": "OpenAI's proofs (2026) of four conjectures on thresholds: the second Kahn–Kalai conjecture (containment thresholds of graphs within a logarithm of the expectation threshold), Talagrand's conjecture that integral and fractional expectation thresholds agree up to a constant, Talagrand's discrete convexity conjecture, and the Ascoli–He–Park–Talagrand decomposition of graphs into pieces that appear at a constant multiple of the integral expectation threshold. Planted resampling, tree covering, multiscale selectors, biased Fourier weights and embedding arguments, all proved in the course.",
